this is not a particle accelerator a  particle accelerator is not some kind of  evil supervillain torture device a  particle accelerator is used for health  safety discovery and for learning more  about our universe you can't see what it  does but you can feel it the question is  can you survive its effects this is what  if and here's what would happen if you  put your head in a particle accelerator  chances are you've probably already been  exposed to accelerated particles before  so how do you feel from x-rays to  airport security treating wastewater and  killing cancer cells particle  accelerators continue to push the  boundaries on the human potential they  might even hold the secret to  time-travel but with great power comes  great responsibility  and the potential for some pretty  serious accidents in 1978 Russian  scientist Anatoly boo Gorsky was  checking in on the malfunctioning u7t  synchrotron which at the time was the  Soviet Union's largest particle  accelerator of course in those days  checking-in meant putting your head in  there and taking a good hard look for  yourself it's hard to imagine what blue  Gorsky might have been looking for since  you can't physically see accelerated  particles they move nearly as fast as  the speed of light when a safety  mechanism failed sending a radioactive  beam of protons through boo gorski's  head the blinding flash of light isa  brighter than a thousand suns according  to him wasn't actually a burst of  accelerated particles that intense light  was the result of 76 billion electron  volts being rammed through Bogor ski  skull for comparison the standard proton  therapy cancer treatment is no more than  250 million electron volts  firing at a speed 300 times less than  what boo Gorsky got and yet but Gorsky  didn't feel any pain the whole thing  happened in an instant but once it was  over boo gorski's face immediately  started swelling he was rushed to the  hospital where doctors told him he  wouldn't live for much longer  but but Gorsky is still alive today half  of his face is paralyzed he's deaf in  one ear and he suffers from epilepsy but  aside from that he lives a pretty normal  life  so our particle accelerators safe to  touch not quite by today's standards the  u7t synchrotron that shot through boo  gorski's head is actually a very weak  particle accelerator in comparison the  Large Hadron Collider which is the  world's largest and highest energy  particle collider fires at about 200  times more power than the u7t this thing  shoes high-energy beams around a ring  that's 27 kilometers long at a speed  that's equivalent to circling the world  7.5 times per second the purpose of this  is to produce high-energy collisions  that will recreate the same conditions  that followed the Big Bang that created  our universe these collisions might  create new particles which we've never  seen before offering up clues to how you  meet how world and everything else came  into existence do you really want to get  your head in the way of that check your  ego before you hurt yourself and don't  interrupt a particle collider from  uncovering more mysteries for all we  know time travel is possible but can you  imagine how weird it would be to meet a  time traveler well that's a story for  another what if
 

